Verzeta Studio is released under a triple-license arrangement:

  - GPL-3.0-or-later  for the differentiated components (RAGP,
                       multi-agent cascade, session router, task and
                       project workflow primitives, heartbeat subagent
                       loop, unified audit trail, canvas runner
                       sandbox).  Canonical text:
                           LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt

  - LGPL-3.0-or-later for the supporting infrastructure (generic
                       models, utilities, CRUD services, wire protocol
                       implementation, UI components, design tokens,
                       build tooling, LLM provider HTTP wrappers,
                       test suite).  Canonical text:
                           LICENSES/LGPL-3.0-or-later.txt

  - Commercial        for organisations that do not want either
                       copyleft variant.  Custom-negotiated; contact
                       via the email in SECURITY.md.

The applicable license for any given source file is declared inline
via an SPDX-License-Identifier header at the top of that file.  The
project is REUSE 3.0 compliant; run `reuse lint` to verify.

A human-readable explanation of the triple-license arrangement,
including which components fall into which tier and what each tier
means for users / forks / integrators / contributors, is in
LICENSING.md at the root of this repository.

The "Verzeta" wordmark and logo are trademarks of the project owner;
their permitted and prohibited uses are described in TRADEMARKS.md.

Contributions are accepted under the Contributor License Agreement
in CLA.md.
